Mail-merge recipient lists: legacy Excel workbooks, text in any common encoding, and Filter and Sort in Edit Recipient List.

**1. `.xls` workbooks.** `.xlsx`/`.xlsm`/`.ods` were already supported (#334); legacy `.xls` (BIFF8) is now read by a pure-Rust reader (`crates/formats/src/sheet/xls.rs`) on the `cfb` crate that was already a dependency. `.xls` is in the file picker (desktop, web, built-in browser) and drag-and-drop. Excel 5.0/95 and password-protected `.xls` give a clear error suggesting `.xlsx`; a CSV saved with an `.xls` name is read as text, an HTML page named `.xls` gets a clear error.

**2. Garbled text.** The screenshot in the issue is a GBK CSV read as Windows-1252. `txt::decode` now detects the legacy encoding when the bytes aren't UTF-8/UTF-16 (GBK/GB18030, Big5, Shift_JIS, EUC-KR, Windows code pages). This also applies when opening plain text, Markdown and LaTeX. New dependencies: `encoding_rs` ((Apache-2.0 OR MIT) AND BSD-3-Clause) and `chardetng` 1.0 (Apache-2.0 OR MIT), which bring `core_detect` and `multiversion_no_op` (MIT/Apache). `mailings.recipients` takes `"encoding"` to force one.

**3. Filter and Sort.** New commands `mailings.filterRecipients` and `mailings.sortRecipients`:
- rules are field + comparison (equal, notEqual, less, greater, lessOrEqual, greaterOrEqual, blank, notBlank, contains, notContains) + value, joined by And/Or (And binds tighter); numbers compare as numbers, text ignores case; `{}` clears filter and sort;
- preview, Finish & Merge and labels use only the matching records, in sort order; editing the list keeps the filter; loading a new list clears it;
- the dialog has a Filter and Sort section (conditions, three sort keys, Clear All), a column with each record's merge order (a dash when filtered out) and "N of M recipients will be merged";
- catalog rows Filter Recipients and Sort Recipients; 24 new strings in every catalog (translations written for this PR, so a native speaker's check is welcome).

