## What was wrong
`layout.pageSetup` with a `section` object applied it without validation. Scripts, MCP agents and the control channel could set a negative, zero, infinite or huge page size, margins larger than the page, absurd column counts, and other values that the dedicated commands (`layout.size`, `layout.margins`, `layout.columns` and others) refuse or clamp. `hostile_params_never_panic` never sent a `section`.

## What changed (`crates/engine/src/cmd/page.rs`)
- `validate_section` checks the given section on a copy **before** anything changes. On an error, nothing is applied, so the section is applied whole or not at all.
- **Refused with an error:**
  - non-finite numbers anywhere;
  - margins that leave less than 36 pt of text room. That's the same rule as `layout.margins`, so tiny pages are refused too.
- **Clamped:**
  - page sides to 7.2–1584 pt;
  - columns to 1–12 with gaps of 0–300 pt (`count` follows the given widths);
  - header and footer distances up to the page height;
  - gutter;
  - line numbering, matching `layout.lineNumbers`;
  - document-grid pitch;
  - page-number start, up to 100,000;
  - footnote and endnote starts, 1–`MAX_NOTE_START`;
  - page-border width (0.25–6 pt, matching `design.pageBorders`) and spacing (0–31 pt).
- `landscape` follows the page sides.
- The limits are shared constants, `MIN_PAGE_SIDE`, `MAX_PAGE_SIDE` and `MIN_TEXT_ROOM`. They're `pub` and identical to #1496's, which also defines them, so whichever PR merges second drops its duplicate.
- The params doc says that `section` replaces the whole section object, headers and footers included.
- Docs: a `ROADMAP.md` progress-log entry, with its status line and revision history.

